    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d515">

                <pb facs="0616" n="548" sameAs="frus:frus1914-20v01/pg548"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">851.857 Su 8/58½</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The French Ambassador</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Jusserand</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1916-04-14">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">April 14, 1916</hi>.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Mr. Secretary</hi>: I send you herewith a
                    translation of a telegr[am] just received.</p>
                <p>My Govt asks that, for the time being, no publicity be given to such information
                    in it which is not public as yet.</p>
                <p>Believe me [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Jusserand</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>You may have noticed that yesterday’s papers (e. g. the <hi
                            rendition="#italic">N. Y. Times</hi>) had a telegr[am] from Berlin
                        stating that the Prussian order “Pour le Mérite” had been conferred on
                        “Lieut. Otto Steinbrinck, the commander of a submarine.”</p>
                </postscript>


                <xi:include href="d515-a1.xml" xpointer="d515-a1"/>
            </div>
